<article class="env-lemma" id="07YK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07YK">Lemma <span data-tag="07YK">98.23.1</span>.</a> Let $A \to k$ be a ring map with $k$ a field. Let $E \in D^-(A)$. Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Ext}}\nolimits ^ i_ A(E, k) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _ k(H^{-i}(E \otimes ^\mathbf {L} k), k)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. Hint: Replace $E$ by a bounded above complex of free $A$-modules and compute both sides. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>